 "interpretation": [
  {
   "heading": "1. Without the mask, the manager adds little",
   "body": "On plain DreamerV3 the v1.2 manager (with the RSSM-2 memory it reads) is +0.77 ± 0.22 over plain on two seeds, but only +0.20 ± 0.24 over RSSM-2 alone, and the second seed ended training below plain. Fixed v1.2 without the mask is +0.33 ± 0.40 over the honest map underneath it. No honest manager run makes a stone tool."
  },
  {
   "heading": "2. The masked scores are largely the mask's",
   "body": "Every v1.x and v2 headline score has the B2 rule mask, which reads the game's action rules and now counts as cheating. Removing it drops fixed v1.2 from 9.03 to 6.13 over 60 worlds (-2.90 ± 0.26) and v2 by about 2.6 achievements in training (v2_norules). Among masked runs, v1.2 leads B2 by +0.50 ± 0.25 on 60 worlds and is level with it in training."
  },
  {
   "heading": "3. Old v1.2 (9.97) was partly luck",
   "body": "Rescored on a second set of 30 worlds it gives 9.50 (9.73 over 60). Its fixed-code reruns average 9.03. Part of the old lead may come from the pre-fix RSSM-2 leak (training saw up to 7 future steps, and the manager plans from those states); one old seed cannot tell (docs/ablations.md)."
  },
  {
   "heading": "4. What would settle the rest",
   "body": "A score for v2_norules, more seeds of v12_nomask and abl_manager, and 60-world scores throughout. The next version of the manager is on family/next (v1.2's named goals on v2)."
  }
 ],
